# The operators the DSC writer's output may use that its own prolog does
# not define.
#
# What that device emits is a program in a language of its own making:
# the prolog defines a short name for each operator the page needs, and
# the page is written in those names. Anything else it emits has to be an
# operator the reader already has, which for this device means
# LanguageLevel 1 -- and every entry below is one, named here so that
# adding a second is a decision somebody takes rather than a token that
# appears.
#
# This exists because the device once emitted an operator its own prolog
# never defined. Nothing had asked for it: the selection concerned is
# written only where the stream is not already carrying it, and only a
# capture starts that record again, so the page that named an operator
# its reader had never heard of was the first page ever to hold a
# captured description. A page that stops at an operator it invented is
# not a difference a byte comparison can see, and the round-trip that
# would have seen it had no workload that reached the emitting path.
#
# The guard reads this both ways. Every bare token the output uses must
# be defined by the prolog, defined by the output itself, or named here.
# And every operator the prolog defines must be reached by the workloads
# below -- so machinery that adds an operator to the prolog and no
# workload to reach it fails here rather than shipping unexercised.

# --- LanguageLevel 1 operators the output uses directly
def             a form's description is named once and called at each placement
gsave           brackets a placement, so the translate it makes is its own
grestore        the other half of that bracket
translate       puts a called description where the placement wants it
showpage        ends the page, which is what a page is for
setpagedevice   states the paper the marks were measured against

# --- names the output writes that are not operators at all
PageSize        the key setpagedevice is given
